@startuml
' ============================================================================
' METADATA
'   author:       TheRobotDrafts Examples
'   description:  Simple traffic-light timing diagram with one lifeline and a state lane.
'   usecase:      Teach lifeline, state/value lane, time axis, state-change waveform.
'   complexity:   simple
'   domain:       Traffic control / embedded timing
' ============================================================================
title Example Timing Diagram - Simple Traffic Light

' A UML timing diagram plots a lifeline's state (or value) against a time axis.
' PlantUML supports timing natively via the `robust` (discrete-state) and
' `concise` (single-value) keywords inside an @startuml block.

robust "TrafficLight" as TL

' The state lane lists the discrete states this lifeline can hold.
@0
TL is "Red"

@5
TL is "Green"

@10
TL is "Yellow"

@12
TL is "Red"

' A time observation labels a point on the time axis (here the cycle restart).
@12 as :cycleRestart

@enduml
